   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": null,
   "text": "On a 64 bit build the classes are 16 bytes apart, so 512 divided by 16 gives 32 of them. Rounding up is what lets a freed block be reused by any other object of about the same size.",
   "originalText": "On a 64 bit build the classes are 16 bytes apart, so 512 divided by 16 gives 32 of them. Rounding up is what lets a freed block be reused by any other object of about the same size.",
